 shipped Sep 23.\n\nLet me also check the drive for shipping-related files? The question is \"Did any order of mine ship recently?\" — mail is the source. Maybe there''s an order tracking file in a drive. But the user asks about \"my order\" — most likely mail.\n\nLet me do a quick aggregateInbox to double-check for anything recent about orders/deliveries in the merged inbox.\n\nActually, to be efficient and thorough, let me just run aggregateInbox with perMailbox 25 to scan recent mail across all mailboxes. That would catch anything order-like.\n\nHmm, but that''s a lot. It''s fine — one call.\n\nLet me do it.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user asked if any of their orders shipped recently.\nI performed several searches: `searchMail` for \"shipment\", \"package\", and \"delivered\".\nI also retrieved the body of the most promising email found.\n\nThe search results showed one relevant email:\n*   **Subject:** \"Your order A-42 has shipped\"\n*   **From:** Acme Store\n*   **Date:** Wed Sep 23 2026 10:00:00 GMT+0000 UTC\n*   **Mailbox:** ana@harness.test\n*   **Body snippet:** \"Good news, your order A-42 is on its way. Track your package\"\n\nAll other searches for \"shipment\", \"package\", or \"delivered\" returned a list of unrelated threads or nothing.\n\nI will now present this finding to the user.The searches for \"package\", \"shipment\", and \"delivered\" returned many \"Re: Long thread\" emails (noise), but the key relevant email is the \"Your order A-42 has shipped\" email from Acme Store.\n\nLet me check if there are other mailboxes in the workspace that might contain shipping info. The search across all mailboxes only returned results from ana@harness.test. But I should check if there are other mailboxes connected. I haven''t listed mailboxes in this conversation. Wait — the first turn mentioned \"3 mailboxes\". Let me list mailboxes to be thorough. Actually, the earlier searches were across all mailboxes (mailboxId omitted), and only ana@harness.test results appeared. But to be safe about \"recent\" and other mailboxes, let me call listMailboxes. Hmm — but the searchMail without mailboxId searches every mailbox. So we''ve covered them. The only shipping email is the Acme Store one.\n\nAlso, \"recently\" — the shipped email is Sep 23, which is ~4 weeks before Oct 19. Is that \"recent\"? It''s the only shipping-related mail. Let me also check the inbox overview to see if anything newer is about an order. Let me do aggregateInbox to check recent inbox items across mailboxes for anything order-related.\n\nActually I already did searchMail \"order\" across all mailboxes, which returned only these. That''s fairly comprehensive. But \"recent\" — maybe a \"delivered\" notice exists elsewhere. The \"delivered\" search returned 0. So: one shipment notification, order A-42, shipped Sep 23.\n\nLet me also check the drive for shipping-related files? The question is \"Did any order of mine ship recently?\" — mail is the source. Maybe there''s an order tracking file in a drive. But the user asks about \"my order\" — most likely mail.\n\nLet me do a quick aggregateInbox to double-check for anything recent about orders/deliveries in the merged inbox.\n\nActually, to be efficient and thorough, let me just run aggregateInbox with perMailbox 25 to scan recent mail across all mailboxes. That would catch anything order-like.\n\nHmm, but that''s a lot. It''s fine — one call.\n\nLet me do it."}],"createdAt":1792374320364},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"mailboxes":1,"count":25,"emails":[{"mailboxId":"4c045289-9c42-53f9-a3d7-2dfac727d3d0","mailbox":"ana@harness.test","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDI4NF0","threadId":"<e2e-privacy-vectors-0001@harness.test>","from":"Shop Weekly","subject":"This week at the shop","date":"Sat Sep 26 2026 08:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"mailboxId":"4c045289-9c42-53f9-a3d7-2dfac727d3d0","mailbox":"ana@h