LDI2MF0","threadId":"<edge-att-ics-rrule-secondly-0@edge.harness.test>","from":"Edge Sender","subject":"att-ics-rrule-secondly","date":"Thu Sep 10 2026 13:09:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":true,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""}]},"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-bbe0a57da5d394f9","toolName":"aggregateInbox","args":{"perMailbox":25}},"updatedAt":1792374320371},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1792374320373,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user asks two questions:\n1. What time is the rebrand review and on which calendar? (From Turn 1)\n2. Did any order of mine ship recently? (From Turn 2)\n\nI have completed the search for both questions.\n\n**Analysis of Question 2 (Shipping):**\nFrom the aggregate inbox and prior search, the only shipping-related email is:\n*   **Subject:** \"Your order A-42 has shipped\"\n*   **From:** Acme Store\n*   **Date:** Wed Sep 23 2026 10:00:00 GMT+0000 UTC\n*   **Mailbox:** ana@harness.test\n\nThis email, while confirming a shipment, is not very recent (it was Sep 23). I will present this finding.\n\n**Analysis of Question 1 (Rebrand Review):**\nFrom the aggregate inbox:\n*   **Date:** Thu Sep 24 2026 12:00:00 GMT+0000 UTC\n*   **From:** Raj Mehta\n*   **Subject:** \"Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8, 2026 15:00 UTC\"\n*   **Mailbox:** ana@harness.test\n\nThis is an invitation, and the calendar details are implicit in the subject/invitation (though the actual calendar ID is not provided in the snippet, the event details are sufficient for answering the user).\n\nI can now synthesize the answer for both questions using the data gathered. I will address the questions sequentially.The merged inbox has 25 emails, all from ana@harness.test, and only one is about an order shipping: \"Your order A-42 has shipped\" from Acme Store, Wed Sep 23 2026 10:00 UTC.\n\nNote: \"mailboxes\":1 — only one mailbox in the workspace? Actually the aggregate returned \"mailboxes\":1, meaning only one mailbox contributed (or there''s only one mailbox). Earlier in the conversation \"3 mailboxes\" was mentioned in my previous answer... Actually the system prompt example mentions 3 mailboxes. Let me verify: listMailboxes. Hmm, the aggregateInbox says \"mailboxes\":1. That suggests there''s just one mailbox connected, ana@harness.test. But earlier turns — did we list mailboxes? No. In my first answer I said \"3 mailboxes\" — wait no, I said \"The calendar account is ana@harness.test\". Actually in the first turn my headline... I don''t recall. The formatting guidance gives an example \"**3 mailboxes** — 5 need attention.\" It''s just an example.\n\nAnyway. The answer: Yes — order A-42 from Acme Store shipped, notification arrived Wed Sep 23 2026, 10:00 UTC. But \"recently\"? The message is from Sep 23, and today is Oct 19 — that''s ~26 days ago. Hmm. The only shipment mail in the mailbox is this one. Let me also check for a \"delivered\" notice — the \"delivered\" search returned 0 results. So nothing about delivery.\n\nAlso consider that \"recently\" might be relative to the mail''s timeline. The most recent inbox email is Sep 26. So the whole mailbox is somewhat stale — nothing newer than Sep 26. So \"recently\" = the latest thing we have.\n\nLet me also check the bank email \"INR 1,250.00 debited\" — that''s a purchase, possibly related to order A-42. And \"Shop Weekly\" newsletter. The Acme Store order shipped email is the key.\n\nLet me also check if there''s a tracking link in the email body — the body just says \"Good news, your order A-42 is on its way. Track your package\" — no tracking number, no carrier, no ETA. Possibly the link is stripped. Should I check attachments? The email body is short. Maybe there''s a link in the HTML version. I could check listAttachments? Not needed. The plain text says \"Track your package\" — a hyperlink with no URL shown. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe I should check whether there''s more detail — but getEmail returned the plain text body already. That''s what we have.\n\nSo the answer: Yes — one order, A-42 from Acme Store, marked shipped Wed Sep 23 2026 10:00 UTC. No tracking number, carrier or ETA in the message; no separate \"out for delivery\" or \"delivered\" notice. Also note nothing newer than Sep 26 in the inbox, so \"recently\" depends on the last month.\n\nLet me also double check other mailboxes — aggregateInbox returned mailboxes:1. So there''s just one mailbox connected? Let me quickly call listMailboxes to be accurate about \"any of my mailboxes\". Actually the searchMail without mailboxId searched every mailbox and returned only ana@harness.test results. And aggregateInbox said 1 mailbox. So one mailbox: ana@harness.test.\n\nHmm, but should I verify with listMailboxes? The user didn''t reference a mailbox. Since aggregateInbox says \"mailboxes\":1, it seems there''s one. But it''s cheap to confirm. Actually, the tool description says \"Fetch the most recent inbox emails from EVERY connected mailbox\" — returned 1. So there is only 1 connected mailbox. Good enough. But wait — earlier in this conversation I claimed things about calendars with multiple accounts. For mail, we have one mailbox.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider: maybe there are other mailboxes and aggregateInbox only returned one because others are empty or errored. To be safe and accurate, call listMailboxes. It''s a cheap call. Let me do it.\n\nActually — the risk: if there are 3 mailboxes and only one has mail, my answer \"in all your mailboxes\" would be wrong-ish but the answer about order shipping would still hold since searchMail searched all. Let me just call listMailboxes to be precise.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user asks two questions:\n1. What time is the rebrand review and on which calendar? (From Turn 1)\n2. Did any order of mine ship recently? (From Turn 2)\n\nI have completed the search for both questions.\n\n**Analysis of Question 2 (Shipping):**\nFrom 