out for delivery\", no \"delivered\", no delay notice. Thread has only one message.\n- Item: Walnut desk lamp; order A-42, Acme Store, shipped Sep 23 10:00 UTC.\n- So status per the only source: last known state \"shipped\" as of Sep 23, promised by Sep 30, nothing since → the trail goes cold after the ship notice. The tracking URL is the only way to get current status, and I can''t fetch it.\n- Drives: nothing.\n\nAlso note the caveat: link points at acme.test/track/... — it''s the merchant''s own tracking page; I can''t open it.\n\nLet me be precise and correct my earlier statement.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The last search of all drives for \"tracking\", \"shipment\", and \"UPS\" yielded no results, confirming that the tracking information is contained only in the shipment email.\n\nI have all the necessary information to answer the user''s question comprehensively, including the tracking details, carrier, and expected delivery window, and also noting the lack of subsequent mail or files providing a delivery status.\n\nFinal answer formulation based on the raw email content.Nothing in drives. Now compose the answer.\n\nImportant: earlier I said the email had no tracking number — because I only read the plain-text body. The tracking details live in a JSON-LD script block in the HTML part. I should correct that.\n\nAnswer:\n- Carrier UPS, tracking number 1Z999AA10123456784, URL.\n- Expected arrival until 2026-09-30 20:00 UTC — that window passed 19 days ago (today Oct 19).\n- No further mail: no \"out for delivery\", no \"delivered\", no delay notice. Thread has only one message.\n- Item: Walnut desk lamp; order A-42, Acme Store, shipped Sep 23 10:00 UTC.\n- So status per the only source: last known state \"shipped\" as of Sep 23, promised by Sep 30, nothing since → the trail goes cold after the ship notice. The tracking URL is the only way to get current status, and I can''t fetch it.\n- Drives: nothing.\n\nAlso note the caveat: link points at acme.test/track/... — it''s the merchant''s own tracking page; I can''t open it.\n\nLet me be precise and correct my earlier statement."}],"createdAt":1792374515352},{"type":"text","text":"**The tracking details exist after all — I misread earlier.** The shipment email''s *plain-text* body says only \"Track your package,\" but the raw message carries a JSON-LD `ParcelDelivery` block in its HTML part with the actual data:\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **Carrier** | UPS |\n| **Tracking number** | `1Z999AA10123456784` |\n| **Tracking URL** | https://acme.test/track/1Z999AA10123456784 |\n| **Item** | Walnut desk lamp |\n| **Order** | A-42 — Acme Store |\n| **Shipped** | Wed 2026-09-23, 10:00 UTC |\n| **Expected arrival** | **by 2026-09-30, 20:00 UTC** |\n\n**The situation, in one line:** it was promised by **Sep 30, 20:00 UTC** — that window closed **19 days ago** — and the trail goes cold there. The shipment notice is the *only* message in the thread (`<e2e-shipment-0001@harness.test>`) and the only order-related mail in the mailbox: no \"out for delivery,\" no \"delayed,\" no \"delivered,\" no second Acme email of any kind. The email has **zero attachments**, so nothing came bundled alongside it.\n\nSo the last confirmed state is \"shipped, expected by Sep 30.\" Whether it actually arrived isn''t recorded anywhere in your workspace — not in mail, and nothing matching tracking/shipment/UPS in any of your **7 drives** either. The only live source is that Acme tracking URL, which I can''t open; your mail stops at the hand-off to UPS. Given the 19-day gap past the expected date, it''s worth checking that link directly or querying Acme with order **A-42**.\n\nIf you''d like, I can draft a chase email to Acme Store (`orders@acme.test`) quoting the tracking number and order — say the word and I''ll put it in Drafts for your review.","createdAt":1792374515352}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**The tracking details exis