s.test: Shop Weekly \"This week at the shop\", Sat Sep 26 2026 08:00 UTC. Sender name literally \"Shop Weekly\", weekly digest format. Body content is a tracking/pixel test — every link is a tracking vector, which is a second reason it reads as a bulk newsletter.\n\nAlso worth flagging: it''s the newest email in the inbox, and it''s the only bulk-style mail. Nothing else matches \"newsletter\", \"digest\", \"roundup\". \"weekly\" matched only this one.\n\nCaveat: only one mailbox exists; and \"Shop Weekly\" may be the only one because there is no promotional bulk sender set otherwise. Also note the mailbox''s `newsletter` label exists — but I can''t list which emails carry it with the tools I have (no label filter tool). Should I search for a tool to filter by label? The instructions say search for capabilities needed. There might be a tool to list emails by label. Let me consider — \"Labels: list every valid label key, apply one, clear one.\" No listing by label described. So no. I''ll note the limitation briefly? Maybe just mention the `newsletter` label exists as the natural home. Keep it short.\n\nFormat per output formatting: group by mailbox header \"## ana@harness.test\" — well, one mailbox. I''ll lead with a headline.\n\nLead: \"**1 mailbox, 1 newsletter-style message**\" or \"Only one thing in your workspace looks like a newsletter.\"\n\nBe concrete.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"I have read the email body for \"This week at the shop\". The body contains boilerplate/HTML content, but the subject and sender (\"Shop Weekly\") strongly indicate it is a marketing/newsletter email. The aggregate inbox scan also confirmed this is the only email fitting this pattern across all visible mailboxes.\n\nI will now present the findings to the user.Newsletter/digest candidates: \"Shop Weekly — This week at the shop\" (Sat Sep 26 2026 08:00 UTC), in ana@harness.test. That''s the only one that reads as a newsletter/digest. Its body is a privacy/tracking-vector test message (\"Every remote reference below points at the harness''s /pixel/* recorder...\" with tracking links) — so it''s a newsletter-shaped message but its content is a tracking test.\n\nEverything else in the inbox is transactional/notification: Harness Bank debit alert, Raj Mehta invitation + Rebrand kickoff (personal/work), Acme shipment, GitHub OTP. The Edge Sender messages are harness edge-case test messages — not newsletters.\n\nSo: exactly one newsletter/digest. I should report that honestly. Also note \"newsletter\" label exists — I could check if anything carries that label, but I don''t have a tool to list emails by label... Actually I don''t. I only know labels exist. I can''t filter by label with the loaded tools. I could mention that the mailbox has a `newsletter` label but no email in my results is labeled with it — but I don''t actually know what''s labeled. Hmm, listEmails returns isRead/isStarred but not labels. So I can''t verify.\n\nLet me just answer.\n\nReport: one newsletter/digest in the workspace, in ana@harness.test: Shop Weekly \"This week at the shop\", Sat Sep 26 2026 08:00 UTC. Sender name literally \"Shop Weekly\", weekly digest format. Body content is a tracking/pixel test — every link is a tracking vector, which is a second reason it reads as a bulk newsletter.\n\nAlso worth flagging: it''s the newest email in the inbox, and it''s the only bulk-style mail. Nothing else matches \"newsletter\", \"digest\", \"roundup\". \"weekly\" matched only this one.\n\nCaveat: only one mailbox exists; and \"Shop Weekly\" may be the only one because there is no promotional bulk sender set otherwise. Also note the mailbox''s `newsletter` label exists — but I can''t list which emails carry it with the tools I have (no label filter tool). Should I search for a tool to filter by label? The instructions say search for capabilities needed. There might be a tool to list emails by label. Let me consider — \"Labels: list every valid label key, apply one, clear one.\" No listing by label described. So no. I''ll note the limitation briefly? Maybe just mention the `newsletter` label exists as the natural home. Keep it short.\n\nFormat per output formatting: group by mailbox header \"## ana@harness.test\" — well, one mailbox. I''ll lead with a headline.\n\nLead: \"**1 mailbox, 1 newsletter-style message**\" or \"Only one thing in your workspace looks like a newsletter.\"\n\nBe concrete."}],"createdAt":1792374887233},{"type":"text","text":"**Only one message in the workspace looks like a newsletter or digest — and it''s a weekly one.**\n\n## ana@harness.test\n\n- **Shop Weekly** — *This week at the shop* — Sat **Sep 26 2026, 08:00 UTC** — the only bulk-sender mail in the inbox. \"Shop Weekly\" is literally a weekly digest brand, and the message is built as one: a stack of remote references and tracking links, with \"Load images\" / blocked-image behavior, a Google-wrapped link and a SendGrid click-tracked link, plus a \"Jump to the bottom\" link. Read status: already read.\n\nThat''s the entire yield. I checked five angles — \"newsletter,\" \"digest,\" \"roundup\" and \"unsubscribe\" all came back either empty or pointing at this same message; **\"digest\" and \"roundup\" returned zero**.\n\nEverything else in the inbox is transactional or 1:1 — not newsletter-shaped:\n\n- **Harness Bank** — INR 1,250.00 debited from a/c \\*\\*4821 — Sep 25\n- **Raj Mehta** — Rebrand kickoff — Sep 21, and *Invitation: Rebrand review* — Sep 24\n- **Acme Store** — Your order A-42 has shipped — Sep 23\n- **GitHub** — sign-in verification code — Sep 22\n- ~90 **Edge Sender** messages (Sep 10) — subject lines like `jsonld-invalid`, `att-pkpass-zip-bomb`, `html-hostile` — those are edge-case test vectors, not digests, despite the bulk-looking subjects.\n\nTwo caveats:\n\n- Your workspace has **one** mailbox, so \"all mailboxes\" is just this one — there''s no second inbox where a digest could be hiding.\n- The inbox does carry a built-in **`newsletter`** label, but the listing tools I have return read/starred status only, not label assignments, so I can''t tell you which messages are actually *tagged* `newsletter` — only which ones read like one. If you want, I can label *This week at the shop* as `newsletter` so it''s sorted correctly from here on.","createdAt":1792374887233}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Only one message in the workspace looks like a newsletter or digest — and it''s a weekly one.**\n\n## ana@harness.test\n\n- **Shop Weekly** — *This week at the shop* — Sat **Sep 26 2026, 08:00 UTC** — the only bulk-sender mail in the inbox. \"Shop Weekly\" is literally a weekly digest brand, and the message is built as one: a stack of remote references and tracking links, with \"Load images\" / blocked-image behavior, a Google-wrapped link and a SendGrid click-tracked link, plus a \"Jump to the bottom\" link. Read status: already read.\n\nThat''s the entire yield. I checked five angles — \"newsletter,\" \"digest,\" \"roundup\" and \"unsubscribe\" all came back either empty or pointing at this same message; **\"digest\" and \"roundup\" returned zero**.\n\nEverything else in the inbox is transactional or 1:1 — not newsletter-shaped:\n\n- **Harness Bank** — INR 1,250.00 debited from a/c \\*\\*4821 — Sep 25\n- **Raj Mehta** — Rebrand kickoff — Sep 21, and *Invitation: Rebrand review* — Sep 24\n- **Acme Store** — Your order A-42 has shipped — Sep 23\n- **GitHub** — sign-in verification code — Sep 22\n- ~90 **Edge Sender** messages (Sep 10) — subject lines like `jsonld-invalid`, `att-pkpass-zip-bomb`, `html-hostile` — those are edge-case test vectors, not digests, despite the bulk-looking subjects.\n\nTwo caveats:\n\n- Your workspace has **one** mailbox, so \"all mailboxes\" is just this one — there''s no second inbox where a digest could be hiding.\n- The inbox does carry a built-in **`newsletter`** label, but the listing tools I have return read/starred status only, not label assignments, so I can''t tell you which messages are actually *tagged* `newsletter` — only which ones read like one. If you want, I can label *This week at the shop* as `newsletter` so it''s sorted correctly from here on."}','assistant','v2','2026-10-19T01:53:32.366Z','7f765568-8c0d-56ce-8b89-105126fefedf');
