t 8 — that''s past. Also maybe upcoming events in early Nov. Let me use a broad window Oct 19 – Nov 2 to see upcoming commitments? The user asked \"this week\", so stick to Oct 19–26 but I could widen slightly. I''ll do Oct 19 00:00 to Oct 26 00:00.\n\nActually, to be safe and helpful, I''ll list events from 2026-10-19T00:00:00Z to 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z.\n\nAlso maybe check read-later list and snoozed/scheduled? \"everything above\" — those weren''t mentioned. The to-do list should be based on mail + calendar. I''ll also check the \"Rebrand\" thread and the invite.\n\nLet me batch these calls:\n1. listEmails page 4 token 135\n2. listEvents timeMin 2026-10-19T00:00:00Z timeMax 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z\n3. getThread for e2e-conversation-0001 (Rebrand kickoff) — mailboxId 4c045289... threadId \"<e2e-conversation-0001@harness.test>\"\n4. getThread for e2e-invite-0001 (invitation)\n\nThat''s 4 calls in one block. Good.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user asked for a prioritized to-do list for the week based on everything above.\n\"Everything above\" includes:\n1.  Inboxes (I''ve retrieved 2 pages and the total count is around 285).\n2.  Workspace members (Ana Silva).\n3.  Calendars (Bulk, Edge cases, Work).\n\n**Current State Analysis:**\n1.  **Inbox Status:** The most recent page of emails (50 emails) are all marked `isRead: false` in the listEmails response (which is counter-intuitive since the initial snippet said \"all were marked isRead: true\", but I must rely on the latest tool output). However, the emails are from \"Edge Sender\" and are all replies to \"Long thread.\" The last page has 50 *unread* emails. This is the primary candidate for tasks/attention.\n2.  **Calendar Status:** I have loaded the tools (`listEvents`, `findMemberEvents`), but I haven''t executed them yet, and I haven''t identified any upcoming events for this week (Oct 19–25).\n3.  **Task Creation:** No actionable items (tasks, documents) were found.\n\n**Goal:** Build a prioritized to-do list.\n\n**Action Plan:**\n1.  **Answer Unread Count:** I have pulled 100 emails so far. The last page has 50 unread. I need to check the total count of unread emails. Since I''ve only paginated, I don''t have the final count. I will report the most prominent actionable item: the unread thread.\n2.  **Find Calendar Events:** Use the loaded tools (`listEvents`) to check for meetings this week (Oct 19–25, 2026) across all calendars (`Bulk`, `Edge cases`, `Work`).\n3.  **Prioritize:** Once I have calendar events and actionable emails, I can generate the list.\n\nLet''s execute the calendar search for \"this week.\"\n\n*   **Start Date:** 2026-10-19T00:00:00Z\n*   **End Date:** 2026-10-25T23:59:59Z\n\nI need to call `listEvents` using the found calendars and the determined time range.Now I found unread emails — a long \"Re: Long thread\" chain from Edge Sender, all isRead: false. Pages 3 shows 50 unread. There''s more (token \"135\"). So the inbox has many unread from this long thread. The user''s first question was \"how many unread emails\" — I should keep paging to count them all. That''s pages 4, 5, 6 (135 → 85 → 35). Actually each page is 50 items. 285 total emails → 6 pages. Pages so far: 285-235 (50), 235-185 (50), 185-135 (50). Next: 135 → 85, 85 → 35.\n\nLet me page through to get the full count. That''s 3 more calls. Also I should list events for this week.\n\nLet me batch: listEmails page 4 (token 135), and listEvents for Oct 19–25 window (or wider: Oct 12–26 to catch this week''s events). Since \"this week\" from Mon Oct 19 to Sun Oct 25, use timeMin 2026-10-19T00:00:00Z, timeMax 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z. Maybe extend to catch the \"Rebrand review\" invite on Oct 8 — that''s past. Also maybe upcoming events in early Nov. Let me use a broad window Oct 19 – Nov 2 to see upcoming commitments? The user asked \"this week\", so stick to Oct 19–26 but I could widen slightly. I''ll do Oct 19 00:00 to Oct 26 00:00.\n\nActually, to be safe and helpful, I''ll list events from 2026-10-19T00:00:00Z to 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z.\n\nAlso maybe check read-later list and snoozed/scheduled? \"everything above\" — those weren''t mentioned. The to-do list should be based on mail + calendar. I''ll also check the \"Rebrand\" thread and the invite.\n\nLet me batch these calls:\n1. listEmails page 4 token 135\n2. listEvents timeMin 2026-10-19T00:00:00Z timeMax 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z\n3. getThread for e2e-conversation-0001 (Rebrand kickoff) — mailboxId 4c045289... threadId \"<e2e-conversation-0001@harness.test>\"\n4. getThread for e2e-invite-0001 (invitation)\n\nThat''s 4 calls in one block. Good."}],"createdAt":1792375276732},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"mailbox":"ana@harness.test","count":50,"nextPageToken":"85","emails":[{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDEzNF0","threadId":"<edge-thread-200-0@edge.harness.test>","from":"Edge Sender","subject":"Re: Long thread","date":"Thu Sep 10 2026 10:28:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":false,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDEzM10","threadId":"<edge-thread-200-0@edge.harness.test>","from":"Edge Sender","subject":"Re: Long thread","date":"Thu Sep 10 2026 10:27:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":false,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDEzMl0","threadId":"<edge-thread-200-0@edge.harness.test>","from":"Edge Sender","subject":"Re: Long thread","date":"Thu Sep 10 2026 10:26:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":false,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDEzMV0","threadId":"<edge-thread-200-0@edge.harness.test>","from":"Edge Sender","subject":"Re: Long thread","date":"Thu Sep 10 2026 10:25:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","isRead":false,"isStarred":false,"snippet":""},{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDEzMF0","threadId":"<edge-thread-200-0@edge.harness.test>","from":"Edge Sender","subject":"Re: Long thread","date":"Thu Sep 10 2026 10:24:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Un